KG42.register("edges-559510b5fa55f9769413fe52",{"id":"S-4d0a35b38e31716b","source":"COMP-464efdadf92efbd8","type":"links","target":"COMP-d5bf3c5421ae2369","evidence_class":"S","scientific_acceptance":false,"relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"paper_ids":["25-p2p_ancillary_bidding"],"assertions":[{"id":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R015::E::v141-c-R015-E001","paper":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding","rule_id":"v141-c-R015","rule_ref":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R015","record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R015-E001","source":"coordination.local_operator","target":"coordination.price_signal","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R015-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E23","v141-b-g02-E09-as-step1-publication","v141-b-g02-E11-as-step3-fairness"]},"evidence_class":"S","provenance_gate":"direct_C_edge_with_constraint_and_source_excerpt","scientific_acceptance":false,"accepted_constraint_ids":["v141-c-R015-C001"],"held_constraint_ids":[],"semantic_review_status":"supported","source":"COMP-464efdadf92efbd8","target":"COMP-d5bf3c5421ae2369","source_occurrence_id":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R015::V::coordination.local_operator","target_occurrence_id":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R015::V::coordination.price_signal","source_unit_id":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-a-M03-ancillary-service::coordination.local_operator","target_unit_id":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-a-M03-ancillary-service::coordination.price_signal","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"Ancillary-service incentive prices published in Step 1 and used for customer bidding in Step 2. | The power utility's coordination of ancillary-service procurement from customers in the P2P energy trading community for the Target Time Period T.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E23","v141-b-g02-E09-as-step1-publication","v141-b-g02-E10-as-step2-bid-form-eq17","v141-b-g02-E11-as-step3-fairness"]},"active":true,"source_signature":"fdc426383ff532854165d39b49ffcbdeb983547b9d75919a937851a08b939ac9","relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"source_science":{"mechanism_id":"v141-a-M03-ancillary-service","source_definition":"The utility, acting as coordinator of the community's ancillary-service procurement, determines which bids are accepted and the quantities procured. Scope: The utility's coordination of ancillary-service procurement from customers in the P2P energy trading community during the ancillary-service Agreement Period. Condition: After collecting customers' ancillary-service bids. Procurement quotas should initially distribute the requested service equally among submitting customers; quotas exceeding customers' bids are redistributed to customers needing additional quotas. Scope: Ancillary-service quota allocation among submitting customers in the P2P energy trading community, separately for each target time slot. Condition: After collecting ancillary-service bids, during quota distribution. Set the customer's final procurement quota equal to its submitted ancillary-service bid. Scope: Step III of ancillary-service procurement allocation, for each submitting customer and target time slot. Condition: The customer's distributed quota is at least its submitted ancillary-service bid. The customer chooses its final procurement quota between zero and its distributed quota, inclusive. Scope: Step III of ancillary-service procurement allocation, for each submitting customer and target time slot. Condition: The customer's distributed quota is below its submitted ancillary-service bid.","target_definition":"The utility, acting as the community's ancillary-service procurement coordinator, issues incentive signals by broadcasting required service quantities and offered service prices to all community customers. Scope: The power utility's coordination of ancillary-service procurement from customers in the P2P energy trading community for the Target Time Period T. Condition: Based on assessment of the future operational status of the power system. The published ancillary-service incentive prices are fixed by the utility. Scope: Ancillary-service incentive prices published in Step 1 and used for customer bidding in Step 2.","constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R015-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The utility, acting as the community's ancillary-service procurement coordinator, issues incentive signals by broadcasting required service quantities and offered service prices to all community customers. Scope: The power utility's coordination of ancillary-service procurement from customers in the P2P energy trading community for the Target Time Period T. Condition: Based on assessment of the future operational status of the power system.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":["theta-DAS","theta-pAS"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E23","v141-b-g02-E09-as-step1-publication","v141-b-g02-E11-as-step3-fairness"]}],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E23","location":{"location_id":"src-212077b9a1-p03-c1r2__v141-a-M03-participation","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"2. Methodological framework ri in In this paper, a framework for ancillary service provision from a ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"After that, in the ancillary service mechanism (shown as the red dashed circle) the power utility will assess its operational needs and issue incentive signals for obtaining ancillary services, and the customers will respond to the signals by submitting bids for providing ancillary services based on the consideration of maximizing their respective economic benefits. The power utility will then assess the bids and make purchase decisions."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E09-as-step1-publication","location":{"location_id":"src-212077b9a1-p06-c1r2__v141-a-M03-bidding","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"of the net load of a customer as a whole, rather than the change of power output/consumption of spec","equation_id":"(15)-(16)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"As the first step, based on the assessment of the future operational status of power systems, the power utility will broadcast the total demand and prices of ancillary services to all the customers in the P2P energy trading community: \\(D^{AS}=\\{D_t^{AS}\\,|\\,t\\in T\\}\\), (15) \\(p^{AS}=\\{p_t^{AS}\\,|\\,t\\in T\\}\\), (16) where \\(D^{AS}\\) is the set of the magnitude (kW) of the ancillary services required for the time slots within the Target Time Period T, and \\(p^{AS}\\) is the set of prices (£/kW/h) that the power utility is willing to pay for the ancillary services provided by the customers. The power utility will also specify the type of ancillary services needed (either 'Type-1 AS' or 'Type-2 AS'). Note that how the power utility decides \\(D^{AS}\\) and \\(p^{AS}\\) involves comprehensive analysis of the power systems managed by the power utility, which is out of the scope of this paper."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E11-as-step3-fairness","location":{"location_id":"src-212077b9a1-p06-c2r1__v141-a-M03-clearing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Applied Energy 278 (2020) 115671 ng After collecting the bids from the customers in the P2P energy a","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"After collecting the bids from the customers in the P2P energy trading community (a time window can be defined in the Agreement Period for this purpose), the power utility needs to decide which of and to what extent the bids are to be accepted/declined. To achieve the fairness, the power utility in principle should distribute the amount of services to be procured averagely on the customers who have submitted the bids. However, the amount of services to be procured from each customer (called as the 'quota') calculated in this way may be higher than some customers' bids, and thus the surplus quotas can be given to other customers in need. With the above considerations, the process detailed in Fig. 3 is proposed for the power utility to decide the amount of services to be procured from the customers."}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"Ancillary-service incentive prices published in Step 1 and used for customer bidding in Step 2. | The power utility's coordination of ancillary-service procurement from customers in the P2P energy trading community for the Target Time Period T.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E23","v141-b-g02-E09-as-step1-publication","v141-b-g02-E10-as-step2-bid-form-eq17","v141-b-g02-E11-as-step3-fairness"]},"source_record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R015-E001","source":"coordination.local_operator","target":"coordination.price_signal","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R015-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E23","v141-b-g02-E09-as-step1-publication","v141-b-g02-E11-as-step3-fairness"]},"paper_scope_note":"CDA, ancillary services, and residual agreement adjustment are kept separate; arrival events, matched orders, and the next ZIP update are not variables at the same time point; reward and compensation costs are different settlement sub-items."}}],"assertion_ids":["25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R015::E::v141-c-R015-E001"]});
